  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "id" : 109,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 2,
    "bounding box" : [ 49.44, 852.403, 237.346, 874.937 ],
    "heading level" : 3,
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 14.04,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "EXPLORINGI DESIGNI OPTIONI"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "id" : 111,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 2,
    "bounding box" : [ 47.68, 829.421, 496.558, 847.86 ],
    "heading level" : 4,
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.649,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "Facts, when combined with ideas, constitute the greatest force in the world."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "id" : 112,
    "page number" : 2,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.4, 724.301, 561.53, 798.06 ],
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "The design process began with several geometries and strategies for the site’s framework. Initial explorations included an organic framework, which would flow with the topography and create unique design responses to the land, but would also lead to less efficient land uses and a city which would lack “urbanity”."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "id" : 113,
    "page number" : 2,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.4, 662.951, 561.778, 718.26 ],
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "A second design incorporated the grid pattern seen in most big cities, like New York. It made more efficient use of the land but had more intersections and created a static and boring city pattern."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "id" : 114,
    "page number" : 2,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.4, 583.151, 561.576, 656.91 ],
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "A third exploration went in the direction of a geometric framework, like Paris, which creates focal elements throughout the site by using circular or octagonal patterns, giving the city a powerful image and identity. The drawback would be the problematic roadway system and inefficient use of land."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "id" : 115,
    "page number" : 2,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.4, 540.311, 561.808, 577.11 ],
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "These initial explorations led to a design, which would synthesize the best elements of each pattern."
  }, {
    "type" : "text block",
    "id" : 116,
