    "bounding box" : [ 49.44, 847.243, 219.458, 868.817 ],
    "heading level" : 3,
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 14.04,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "RESULTANT FRAMEWORK"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "id" : 125,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 3,
    "bounding box" : [ 47.68, 823.301, 515.178, 841.74 ],
    "heading level" : 4,
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.649,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "The object of art is to crystalize emotion into thought, and then to fix in form."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "id" : 126,
    "page number" : 3,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.4, 724.181, 561.756, 816.3 ],
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "Following the initial explorations, synthesis of the most attractive aspects of each pattern resulted in hybrid geometric and grid framework. The final framework is a combination of the practicality of a grid pattern, the clarity and beauty of a strong geometric core, and the use of organic forms at the edges of the site to transition to adjacent open spaces and effectively deal with the meandering property boundaries."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "id" : 127,
    "page number" : 3,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.4, 625.871, 561.492, 718.14 ],
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "The underlying dimensional structure of Fort Bonifacio is a grid focused on the Central commons, with the East-West axis and Bonifacio Boulevard serving as the primary axes of the city. Overlaying this grid is the geometry of four (4) concentric circles and the singular organic form, which stretches from McKinley Road to the institutional area."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "id" : 128,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 3,
    "bounding box" : [ 49.44, 597.973, 201.106, 620.507 ],
    "heading level" : 3,
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 14.04,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "STRATEGICI LOCATIONI"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "id" : 130,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 3,
    "bounding box" : [ 47.68, 574.871, 482.878, 593.31 ],
    "heading level" : 4,
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.649,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "The three most important things in real state: location, location, location."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "id" : 131,
    "page number" : 3,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.4, 438.891, 561.7, 567.99 ],
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "Fort Bonifacio is 440 contiguous hectares of land located in Metro Manila’s most strategic location. It is bordered by the country’s three(3) largest road arteries: the South Luzon Expressway, EDSA and C-5. It is destined to become the country’s primary business gateway, being just minutes away from the Ninoy Aquino International Airport. It is likewise less than 2 kilometers from Metro Manila’s other business centers, where the highest priced properties are located, as well as being adjacent to Forbes Park and Dasmariñas Village, the city’s most expensive residential districts."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "id" : 132,
    "page number" : 3,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.4, 359.091, 561.496, 432.85 ],
    "font" : "LucidaSansUnicode",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.502]",
    "content" : "Fort Bonifacio can also lay claim to having the best views in Metropolitan Manila. At surface, Fort Bonifacio is cradled by Manila Golf and the American Battle Memorial. At elevation, the city gives superb views of Laguna Lake, Manila Bay and its sunset , as well as the surrounding mountain ranges."
  }, {
